-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/eaf07084-5bcd-5aa0-8eeb-4c602bd3aae0
-- title:
--   Ramification depth computed from a single algebra generator
-- statement:
--   The module records the standard monogenicity device for ramification filtrations. The starting point is a divisibility lemma: for a commutative $A$-algebra $R$ and $x,y \in R$, $x-y$ divides $\mathrm{aeval}\,x\,p - \mathrm{aeval}\,y\,p$ for every $p \in A[X]$ ([`Polynomial.sub_dvd_aeval_sub`](../def/Mathlib_RingTheory_Valuation_LowerRamificationGroupGenerator.html#L8)). Consequently, for an $A$-algebra endomorphism $\sigma$ of $R$ and $r \in A[x]$ one has $\sigma x - x \mid \sigma r - r$, and if $A[x] = R$ (i.e. `Algebra.adjoin A {x} = ⊤`) this holds for all $r \in R$. The same statements are transported to a monoid $G$ acting on $R$ by ring automorphisms, under the hypothesis that the chosen $\sigma \in G$ fixes the image of $A$ pointwise, $\sigma \cdot \mathrm{algebraMap}_{A,R}(a) = \mathrm{algebraMap}_{A,R}(a)$.
--
--   For $R$ a discrete valuation ring with additive valuation `addVal R`, a group $G$ acting by ring automorphisms and an $A$-algebra structure on $R$, the consequence is that $\mathrm{addVal}(\sigma x - x) \le \mathrm{addVal}(\sigma r - r)$ for all $r$, hence that the ramification depth $\mathrm{ramificationDepth}\,R\,G\,\sigma = \inf_{r \in R} \mathrm{addVal}(\sigma r - r)$ is attained at any single generator: it equals $\mathrm{addVal}(\sigma x - x)$ whenever $A[x] = R$ and $\sigma$ fixes $A$. In particular the value $\mathrm{addVal}(\sigma x - x)$ is independent of the generator chosen, and membership of $\sigma$ in the $i$-th lower ramification group (the inertia subgroup of $\mathfrak{m}^{i+1}$, i.e. $\sigma r - r \in \mathfrak{m}^{i+1}$ for all $r$) is equivalent to $i+1 \le \mathrm{addVal}(\sigma x - x)$ in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$, and equivalently to $\sigma x - x \in \mathfrak{m}^{i+1}$. A variant replaces the fixing hypothesis by an `SMulCommClass G A R` assumption, and two further corollaries restate the depth formula and the membership criterion for a discretely valued valuation subring $A \subseteq L$ with $L/K$ an extension of fields, with $G$ the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $K$.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** The notions `ramificationDepth` and `lowerRamificationGroup` used here are the project's, defined in the imported modules on top of Mathlib's `Ideal.inertia`, `IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal` and `ValuationSubring.decompositionSubgroup`; the first lemma is the `aeval` form of Mathlib's `Polynomial.sub_dvd_eval_sub`.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These criteria are the computational entry point to the lower ramification filtration: once the valuation ring is generated by one element over the base, ramification depths and the groups $G_i$ are read off from the valuation of $\sigma x - x$ for that generator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_Mathlib_RingTheory_Valuation_LowerRamificationGroupGenerator.lean

